WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.703
-There's just
a little over one day left

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.204
in the presidency
of Donald Trump.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:07.740
And as we survey the damage
he'll leave behind

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.809
and the impeachment trial
he faces ahead,

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.445
we're learning more about
the insurrection he incited,

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.747
his premeditated plan
to steal the election,

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.850
and the complicity of virtually
the entire Republican Party.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.420
Oh, and also Trump met
with the My Pillow guy.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.588
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:26.092
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.794
On Friday, as an incoming
Democratic administration

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:31.230
was preparing
for the second time in 12 years

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.232
to take the reins
from a deeply unpopular

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:36.402
outgoing Republican president
who left the nation in ruins,

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.171
we got a revealing split screen

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.272
of what our politics
are like right now

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:42.174
with the Trump White House
being boxed up

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:44.878
and the Biden administration
preparing to take over.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.913
We were presented with
a very stark choice

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.447
for where we want to go
as a country.

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.649
On the one hand,
President-Elect Biden

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:52.051
unveiled a five-point plan

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.886
to overhaul
the botched vaccine rollout

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:56.255
and stem the tide of
the deadly coronavirus pandemic

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:58.991
that's been willfully neglected
by the Trump White House.

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:00.927 line:60%
-President-Elect Joe Biden
is pushing ahead

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.929 line:60%
with plans to activate
the Defense Production Act

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.564 line:60%
and ramp up
the national supply

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.865 line:64%
of the coronavirus vaccine.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.967 line:15%
-The incoming administration
pledging to get

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.501 line:21%
100 million doses

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:12.905 line:15%
in the first 100 days
after Joe Biden takes office.

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:15.208 line:15%
The plan including
mass vaccination centers

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.343 line:15%
and training
an Army of vaccinators,

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.844 line:21%
among other steps.

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:22.115
-And to staff up these centers,
we will mobilize

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:25.418
thousands of clinical and
nonclinical professionals.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:28.120
This will be one of the most
challenging operational efforts

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.255
ever undertaken by our country.

00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:33.292
But you have my word:

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.295
we will manage the hell
out of this operation.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:37.630
-Whenever he's
giving a pep talk,

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.764
Biden's got the vibe

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:40.366
of a retired
high school football coach

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.168
taking his grandkids
to Chuck E. Cheese.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.069
"Alright, let's draw it up
on the chalkboard.

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:46.472
Taylor, you're gonna run
the slant route to Super Slide.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.508
Katie, you're gonna post up
at the arcade.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.175
And, Tim, you're gonna go deep
in the ball pit,

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:52.312
but remember you must come back
in 30 minutes

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:55.848
so we can manage the hell
out of some pizza!"

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.850
But I got to say, the whole
"President a plan" thing

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.686
is a genuine relief after
four years of Dr. Head Injury

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.121
over here swinging wildly

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:05.024
between "Everything is fine" and
"We're all gonna die."

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:08.160
"This coronavirus, it's just
gonna go away, folks.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.563
It's gonna go away.
And as soon as it does,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.765
the Antifa caravans
are gonna arrive,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.899
and it's not gonna be pretty.

00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:15.869
You'll be praying
for coronavirus

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.670
when the caravans show up."

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.506
So, that's what the incoming
President was doing on Friday.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:21.874
What about
the outgoing president?

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:23.142
Who was he meeting with?

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:25.711
Can I assume it was also
an expert of some kind?

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:28.180
Perhaps a doctor, a scientist,
or maybe it was someone

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.117
who specializes in
public health infrastructure

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.685
and mass vaccination planning?

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.220
Ooh, wouldn't that be great?
You know what?

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.457
Let me just set up the old
chin cradle and find out.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:40.659 line:45%
-One of the president's
visitors today, Mike Lindell,

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:43.129 line:45%
the founder of My Pillow,
was seen over here

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.964 line:45%
at the White House,
outside the West Wing.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.799 line:53%
The White House official
did tell me, Wolf,

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.502 line:53%
that it is believed that
the president and Lindell met.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.038 line:53%
-A "Washington Post"
photographer got a close-up

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:54.273 line:53%
of the notes that he
was carrying with him.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.008 line:53%
And, Jake, when you
zoom in on them,

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:58.277 line:53%
you can see that he is talking
about the election.

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:00.713 line:53%
Things like martial law
are mentioned.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.983 line:53%
The words "taken immediately
to save the Constitution."

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.619 line:15%
-The guy from My Pillow
is carrying documents

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.654 line:15%
and talking
to President Trump --

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.990 line:15%
presumably about
declaring martial law.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.492
-You know what?
I think this chin cradle

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:13.926
is bad luck.
I'm gonna stop using it.

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:16.062
But that's just great.
The My Pillow guy,

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:19.198
AKA The Notorious MPG,
who, it should be noted,

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.867
is not even good at pillows,
is walking into the White House

00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:24.069
with an insane suggestion
for the president.

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:26.672
What's next? The ShamWow Guy
strolling in

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:29.175
with a notepad that says
"Become an X-Man?"

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:32.344
Also, not to be judgmental,
but if I was going to a meeting

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:35.381
to tell the president
he should declare martial law,

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.883
I might not
need to write it down.

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:39.919
Was there a risk you were gonna
forget that part?

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.587
"Good meeting, Mike.
Anything else?"

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:42.888
"Uh, let's see, I told you

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:44.857
Hugo Chávez
hacked the elections.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.259
Filled you in on our new
three-ply mattress topper.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:49.194
You know, I'm sorry,
Mr. President.

00:03:49.194 --> 00:03:51.897
Let me, uh, check my notes.
Oh, duh-dur!

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:54.667
I forgot you should
declare martial law.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.036
This is why
I write things down!"

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.637
Also, just
a random thought here,

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:00.906
but this is one of those moments
where I'm reminded

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:03.275
that there were voters --
not many, but some --

00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:05.644
who were torn
between Trump and Biden.

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:07.847
Hmm, the guy with
a five-point plan

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.816
to build the infrastructure
for mass vaccination

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:13.052
during a deadly pandemic,
or a guy whose best friend

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.254
is obviously
a psychotic pillow salesman.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:16.756
It's a coin flip!"

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:19.225
Although I think my favorite
detail from the Lindell meeting

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:22.228
involves White House counsel
Pat Cipollone,

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.131
who met with Lindell after a
series of White House officials

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.934
basically kept trying to pass
Lindell off to someone else.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.836 line:0%
First, Trump met with Lindell,
but it was a brief meeting.

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:33.171 line:0%
Trump sent him upstairs to the
White House counsel's office.

00:04:33.171 --> 00:04:34.773 line:0%
Lindell was then escorted

00:04:34.773 --> 00:04:36.576 line:0%
by the national security
adviser, Robert O'Brien.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.344 line:0%
O'Brien, seeking
to end the conversation,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.346 line:0%
said if there was evidence
of what he was saying,

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.147 line:0%
it should go
to White House counsel,

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:44.750 line:0%
and he steered Lindell upstairs
to the counsel's office.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.685 line:0%
Then, once Lindell
got to the counsel's office,

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:49.955 line:0%
Lindell spoke sharply
to one of Cipollone's assistants

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:51.223 line:0%
after he was brought upstairs.

00:04:51.223 --> 00:04:53.226 line:0%
Cipollone told him
he wouldn't speak to him

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.927 line:0%
until Lindell apologized to her.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.129 line:0%
So everyone just kept trying
to get rid of him

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.564 line:0%
by passing him off
to someone else.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.267
In fact, Lindell is still in
the White House, as we speak,

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.136
getting shunted
from office to office.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:05.138
The White House chef
just got done telling him

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.471
what kind of flour they use,

00:05:06.471 --> 00:05:08.541
and now he's pitching his plan
to the lawnmower kid.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:11.043
"Do you know how to declare
martial law?!"

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:14.813
You know, you could also just
not let him into the building.

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:16.716
Why is it easier
to get into the White House

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:18.684
than a restaurant in Chelsea
during brunch?

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.486
Also I'm glad Cipollone stood up
for his assistant.

00:05:21.486 --> 00:05:23.556
But that's
the line you're drawing?

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.992
"I'm sorry, but I simply
will not allow you

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.761
to spread your deranged theories
about Hugo Chávez

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.662
coming back from the dead
to hack the election

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:33.232
unless you learn some manners!"

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.667
"I'm sorry.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.503
Will you declare martial law...
please?"

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.772
This whole situation
is so perfectly indicative

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:40.940
of the entire Trump era.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.908
Instead of just saying,
"No! Get out!"

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:45.111
they all go to absurd lengths
to debase themselves

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:47.580
to accommodate Trump and
his circle of crazy old men

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.683
with mysteriously brown hair.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.585
That's why he had to invent
his own pillow.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:54.253
All the other ones
look like a saddle

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:56.622
after three nights.
And indulging Trump,

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.424
as we've learned,
has real-world consequences.

00:05:59.424 --> 00:06:02.294
Thanks to Trump and his allies
in the GOP and right-wing media

00:06:02.294 --> 00:06:04.497
repeating their deranged lies
about the election,

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:07.900
a new CNN poll found
that 75% of Republicans

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.503
believe Biden isn't
the legitimate president.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:13.372
Virtually the entirety
of the Republican Party,

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:14.740
with only a few exceptions,

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.143
like the 10 Republicans
who voted for the impeachment,

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.945
has taken a hard turn
against democracy

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.914
and towards authoritarianism.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.716
And instead of standing up
and saying clearly

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.618
that we need to tell the truth
about the election

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:28.154
and ostracize anyone
who doesn't accept it,

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:31.691
senior Republicans are insisting
that we all need to capitulate

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:34.226
to Trump in order
to appease his lunatic base.

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:36.762
Lindsey Graham, for example,
pleaded with his party

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:38.898
not to hold Trump accountable
for inciting

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.967
the violent insurrection
at the Capitol.

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:44.070 line:53%
-Mr. President, your policies
will stand the test of time.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.939 line:53%
You're the most important figure
in the Republican Party.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:49.207 line:53%
You can shape
the direction of the party,

00:06:49.207 --> 00:06:50.943 line:57%
keep your movement alive.

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:53.946 line:53%
If we embrace an
unconstitutional impeachment

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.482 line:53%
of Donald Trump
after he's out of office,

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.384 line:57%
it will destroy the party.

00:06:58.384 --> 00:07:01.320 line:53%
The Republican Party
wants to move forward.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.989 line:53%
President Trump's going to be
the most important voice

00:07:03.989 --> 00:07:06.458 line:53%
in the Republican Party
for a long time to come.

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:08.260 line:53%
He's going to accept
responsibility

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.963 line:53%
for his part on
January the 6th,

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.632 line:53%
but impeaching him
after he leaves office

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.434 line:57%
is not only unconstitutional,

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:19.004 line:53%
from a Republican point of view,
it would destroy our party.

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:21.073
-You know what?
If holding Trump accountable

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:22.741
for inciting
violent insurrection

00:07:22.741 --> 00:07:24.843
destroys the Republican Party,
then so be it.

00:07:24.843 --> 00:07:27.279
You want to build it back up
again into something decent,

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:29.382
be my guest.
But now Lindsey Graham

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:31.317
is like an admiral
in the Galactic Empire,

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:33.552
saying, "Guys, don't leave
the exhaust port open,

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:34.953
or it will destroy
the Death Star."

00:07:34.953 --> 00:07:37.923
Also, what do you mean
Donald Trump's going to accept

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:40.893
responsibility for
his part on January 6th?

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:42.928
Are you nuts?
Just because you sound like

00:07:42.928 --> 00:07:44.930
a character
in a Tennessee Williams play

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.798
doesn't mean you have to
act like one, too.

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:48.868
"Oh, what's Lindsey
doin' on the front porch?"

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.504
"Oh, he's still out there
waiting for Donald Trump

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.739
to accept responsibility
for January 6th.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:56.909
Oh, Lindsey!
When will you ever learn?"

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.277
"He's comin', Mama.

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:00.812
He knows he was wrong,
and he's comin'.

00:08:00.812 --> 00:08:03.416
Isn't that right,
Glass Unicorn?"

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:05.684
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.684 --> 00:08:07.787
At this point, it's difficult
to ignore the reality

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:09.755
that the Republican Party is,
from the top down,

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:12.391
a threat to our democracy.
Trump is leaving the nation

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.459
in ruins,
with the lowest approval rating

00:08:14.459 --> 00:08:16.028
of any President
in modern history;

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:18.998
400,000 Americans have died
in the coronavirus pandemic;

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.500
there are 3 million fewer jobs
than when Trump took office;

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.735
the vaccine rollout
is a disaster;

00:08:23.735 --> 00:08:25.137
a violent insurrection

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:27.439
fueled by a deranged
authoritarian movement

00:08:27.439 --> 00:08:29.708
killed multiple people,
ransacked the Capitol,

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:31.510
and nearly toppled
American democracy;

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.612
there are 20,000 troops
guarding D.C.;

00:08:33.612 --> 00:08:36.649
and instead of banishing Trump
from politics to jail

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:39.886
or to his golf course, where
he'd be glimpsed only rarely,

00:08:39.886 --> 00:08:42.688
through blurry photos, like
some sort of fairway Bigfoot,

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:44.790
Lindsey Graham wants him
to remain a leader

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.825
in the Republican Party
for years to come.

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:48.961
You know what that makes you,
Lindsey? A coconspirator.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.596
It's like if a guy
on your bowling team

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:52.331
turned out to be a cannibal,
and you said,

00:08:52.331 --> 00:08:54.567
"Don't turn him in.
The championship's next week.

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:58.270
So what if he ate Carl?
Carl was dead weight anyway."

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:01.339
Seriously, is there anyone
slimier than Lindsey Graham?

00:09:01.339 --> 00:09:04.877
He called Trump a crazy bigot
who was unfit for office;

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:08.247
warned accurately that if
the GOP nominated Trump,

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:10.182
they'd get destroyed
and deserve it;

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:11.684
then did an about-face
and became

00:09:11.684 --> 00:09:13.952
Trump's loyal foot soldier,
golf buddy, and Mini-Me;

00:09:13.952 --> 00:09:15.821 line:0%
then, after the insurrection,

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:18.090 line:0%
said, "Count me out.
Enough is enough";

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.393 line:0%
then flew with Trump
on Air Force One;

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:22.728
and now he's saying
we shouldn't impeach him.

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:24.730
He's like a hostage negotiator
who says,

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.432
"You want a helicopter
and $1 million?

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:28.567
I'll give you something
better -- me."

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:31.236
These people had four years
rationalizing and excusing

00:09:31.236 --> 00:09:33.239
Trump's behavior because
they were all in on it.

00:09:33.239 --> 00:09:36.041
Long ago, they decided to
disgrace themselves

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:38.978
and service this monstrous
and irredeemable man,

00:09:38.978 --> 00:09:40.646
and this dismantling
of our democracy

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:42.281
is just the culmination
of all that.

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:43.715
And even the ones

00:09:43.715 --> 00:09:46.285
who didn't technically object
to the electoral votes

00:09:46.285 --> 00:09:49.254
the way Josh Hawley or Ted Cruz
did are complicit.

00:09:49.254 --> 00:09:51.723
It's a moral rot that runs
through virtually the entirety

00:09:51.723 --> 00:09:53.926
of the Republican Party
and conservative movement.

00:09:53.926 --> 00:09:56.328
You might remember
that when it first became clear

00:09:56.328 --> 00:09:59.164
Trump had lost the election,
more than a few Republicans said

00:09:59.164 --> 00:10:00.933
there was no harm
in indulging him.

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:02.434
Remember, we knew in advance

00:10:02.434 --> 00:10:04.170
it would take days
to count the votes,

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.372
and it was clear
soon after the election

00:10:06.372 --> 00:10:08.907
that Joe Biden hadn't just won,
he won handily,

00:10:08.907 --> 00:10:11.009
with 7 million more votes
across the country

00:10:11.009 --> 00:10:12.744
and a total of
306 electoral votes,

00:10:12.744 --> 00:10:14.946
including states Republicans
had held for decades,

00:10:14.946 --> 00:10:16.382
like Georgia and Arizona.

00:10:16.382 --> 00:10:20.051
And yet Republicans insisted
on going to absurd lengths

00:10:20.051 --> 00:10:22.655
to pretend that the result
was still up in the air.

00:10:22.655 --> 00:10:25.591
They were like Browns fans
holding out hope for a comeback

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:27.460
on Monday morning.
"You're telling me

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:31.229
a 35-year-old backup quarterback
runs for 13 yards

00:10:31.229 --> 00:10:32.832
with a minute left
to ice the game?

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:35.200
I call fraud."
And I'm sorry, Browns fans.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.169
I was nice last week,
but you beat my Steelers,

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:40.773 line:53%
and now you get
a Gentle Payback Burn.

00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:42.774 line:53%
Even aside from propagating
the malicious lie

00:10:42.774 --> 00:10:44.877
that the election was stolen,
they kept repeating

00:10:44.877 --> 00:10:47.212
the ridiculous talking point
that Trump had every right

00:10:47.212 --> 00:10:49.447
to pursue his legal objections,
which is a little bit

00:10:49.447 --> 00:10:51.783
like Browns fans saying they
have a right to protest

00:10:51.783 --> 00:10:53.585
the results of the game
after the Super Bowl.

00:10:53.585 --> 00:10:55.587
Okay, okay, the second burn
was unnecessary,

00:10:55.587 --> 00:10:57.489
and I apologize
because that's piling on,

00:10:57.489 --> 00:10:58.857
kind of like
how the Chiefs defense

00:10:58.857 --> 00:11:00.259
piled on your quarterback
last night.

00:11:00.259 --> 00:11:02.527
Okay, no, I'm sorry!
I'm sad about the Steelers!

00:11:02.527 --> 00:11:05.264
It's not about you!

00:11:05.264 --> 00:11:10.636
It's about me! My problem!
I can't let go!

00:11:10.636 --> 00:11:12.838
[ Laughter ]

00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:14.874
I don't like being like this!

00:11:14.874 --> 00:11:17.276
[ Laughter ]

00:11:17.276 --> 00:11:18.877
Anyway, the point is,
Republicans did

00:11:18.877 --> 00:11:20.746
what they've been doing
for five years now --

00:11:20.746 --> 00:11:22.848
indulging Trump,
hoping they'll be able

00:11:22.848 --> 00:11:25.050
to appease him and his voters
while getting

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.286
everything they want
with no damage to the system --

00:11:27.286 --> 00:11:29.555
a strategy that's worked out
great so far.

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:31.256
In fact, they went
to absurd lengths

00:11:31.256 --> 00:11:33.225
to humiliate themselves
in service of a man

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:35.393
they knew to be craven and
sadistic and deranged.

00:11:35.393 --> 00:11:37.930
You might remember one of the
most infamous examples

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:39.898
from North Dakota
Senator Kevin Cramer,

00:11:39.898 --> 00:11:42.935
who was asked if he considered
Joe Biden the president-elect

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:46.104
after the Electoral College
certified Joe Biden's win.

00:11:46.104 --> 00:11:47.873
And this was
Cramer's full answer.

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:24.710 line:0%
at this point, so we'll see
how the e-mails turn out."

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:27.145
Oh, my God, that was like
if Gary Busey

00:12:27.145 --> 00:12:30.149
body-swapped into an 8th grader
who was just about to do

00:12:30.149 --> 00:12:32.184
his oral report
on the Electoral College.

00:12:32.184 --> 00:12:34.186
"Ugh! What now?!"

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:36.087 line:0%
These guys are
such spineless weasels

00:12:36.087 --> 00:12:37.690 line:0%
that if you ask them
one simple question

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:38.791 line:0%
about who won the election,

00:12:38.791 --> 00:12:40.726 line:0%
they turn into
malfunctioning droids.

00:12:40.726 --> 00:12:43.295 line:0%
He sounds like an Echo that
just got dropped in the toilet.

00:12:43.295 --> 00:12:45.997
"Alexa, is Joe Biden
the president-elect?"

00:12:45.997 --> 00:12:48.166
-Well, it seems to me
that being elected

00:12:48.166 --> 00:12:50.302
by the Electoral College
is a threshold

00:12:50.302 --> 00:12:52.438
where a title like that is
probably most appropriate --

00:12:52.438 --> 00:12:55.174
-Okay, never mind, never mind.
Just play Taylor Swift.

00:12:55.174 --> 00:12:57.309
-Playing "PopoZao"
by Kevin Federline.

00:12:57.309 --> 00:12:59.044
-No, no, no, play Taylor Swift.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:01.212
-Playing "PopoZao"
by Kevin Federline.

00:13:01.212 --> 00:13:03.949
-I said, "Play Taylor Swift."
-Playing Taylor Swift.

00:13:03.949 --> 00:13:05.684
-Thank you.
-Covering "PopoZao"

00:13:05.684 --> 00:13:07.720
by Kevin Federline.
-Alexa!

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.488
[ Laughter ]

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:11.356
Now Cramer and Graham
are the kinds of guys

00:13:11.356 --> 00:13:13.725
who don't get as much attention
as, say, Hawley and Cruz,

00:13:13.725 --> 00:13:15.360
because they just went along
for the ride

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:16.795
while Hawley and Cruz
led the way.

00:13:16.795 --> 00:13:19.031
For example, new footage
from "The New Yorker" reveals

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:21.499
that once the insurrectionists
got inside the Senate chamber,

00:13:21.499 --> 00:13:23.636
they made clear they
considered Cruz an ally.

00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:25.837 line:68%
-Look here, look.
-Ted Cruz's objections

00:13:25.837 --> 00:13:27.505 line:68%
to Arizona.
-His objection.

00:13:27.505 --> 00:13:29.441 line:68%
He was gonna sell us out
all along.

00:13:29.441 --> 00:13:31.043 line:71%
-Really? [Bleep]

00:13:31.043 --> 00:13:33.212 line:68%
-Objection to counting
electoral votes

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:35.781 line:68%
on the state of Arizona.
-Can I get a photo of that?

00:13:35.781 --> 00:13:38.284 line:71%
[ Indistinct conversation ]

00:13:45.257 --> 00:13:47.326 line:71%
-[Bleep].

00:13:53.699 --> 00:13:55.467
-Cool shout-out, Ted.
Congrats.

00:13:55.467 --> 00:13:57.436
That's like
the seditionist version

00:13:57.436 --> 00:14:00.439
of getting a song dedicated
to you by the morning zoo crew.

00:14:00.439 --> 00:14:02.808
"This insurrection goes out
to Ted from Calgary.

00:14:02.808 --> 00:14:05.243
Thanks for helping us
overthrow a democracy, Ted!"

00:14:05.243 --> 00:14:07.479
[ Air horn blowing ]

00:14:07.479 --> 00:14:08.914
[ Laughter ]

00:14:08.914 --> 00:14:10.816
"This Taylor Swift cover
of "PopoZao"

00:14:10.816 --> 00:14:13.952
is going out to Ted Cruz."
[ Laughter ]

00:14:13.952 --> 00:14:16.154
Trump telegraphed for months
that he was going to do

00:14:16.154 --> 00:14:18.223
exactly what he did --
try to steal the election

00:14:18.223 --> 00:14:19.724
and refuse to accept
the outcome.

00:14:19.724 --> 00:14:21.893
And over the weekend,
we learned from new reporting

00:14:21.893 --> 00:14:24.063
what we basically already knew
from Trump's own words

00:14:24.063 --> 00:14:25.464
and actions --
that the attempt

00:14:25.464 --> 00:14:27.532
to steal the election
was premeditated and planned

00:14:27.532 --> 00:14:29.235
long in advance.
According to Axios...

00:14:55.961 --> 00:14:57.562
Oh, really, you were stunned?

00:14:57.562 --> 00:15:00.131
That's like watching
that Werner Herzog documentary

00:15:00.131 --> 00:15:02.300
about the dude who
hangs out with grizzly bears

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:04.770
and being stunned when he
gets eaten by a grizzly bear.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.905
You think Werner's gonna
make a documentary

00:15:06.905 --> 00:15:09.174
where the dude and the bear
end up as buddies?

00:15:09.174 --> 00:15:13.512
"And as I watched man and bear
frolic in the stream,

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:17.349
their friendship unbreakable,
I realized something

00:15:17.349 --> 00:15:20.719
to be clear.
This movie was a dud."

00:15:20.719 --> 00:15:21.887
[ Laughter ]

00:15:21.887 --> 00:15:23.422
It's like, I love
when they bring back

00:15:23.422 --> 00:15:25.090
characters from season one
for the finale.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.558
Now they're gonna have to call
Reince Priebus

00:15:26.558 --> 00:15:28.393
as a witness
in the impeachment trial.

00:15:28.393 --> 00:15:29.928
It's gonna be like
the "Seinfeld" finale.

00:15:29.928 --> 00:15:31.396
Oh, you know who else
is gonna be a witness?

00:15:31.396 --> 00:15:32.531
Trump's lawyer.

00:15:32.531 --> 00:15:34.700 line:15%
-New this morning, Rudy Giuliani
now says

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.802 line:15%
that he will not represent
President Trump

00:15:36.802 --> 00:15:38.003 line:21%
during his impeachment trial.

00:15:38.003 --> 00:15:39.671 line:15%
The president's
personal attorney says

00:15:39.671 --> 00:15:41.840 line:15%
that he can not be part of
the president's legal team,

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.343 line:15%
because he also gave a speech
to supporters

00:15:44.343 --> 00:15:46.678 line:15%
moments before the siege
on the Capitol.

00:15:46.678 --> 00:15:48.379 line:15%
During his speech,
he told crowds

00:15:48.379 --> 00:15:51.016 line:21%
to engage in "trial by combat."

00:15:51.016 --> 00:15:54.153 line:15%
Giuliani says this makes him
a witness to the day's events.

00:15:54.153 --> 00:15:57.422
-Trump is such a criminal,
his lawyers are also criminals.

00:15:57.422 --> 00:16:00.425
"Your honor, my client
isn't the murderer; I am.

00:16:00.425 --> 00:16:02.928
Just ask my client -- he was
there, because he helped me.

00:16:02.928 --> 00:16:04.829
It's gonna be impossible
for Trump to find

00:16:04.829 --> 00:16:06.598
a lawyer who
isn't also an accomplice.

00:16:06.598 --> 00:16:09.635
I mean, no credible lawyer wants
to get anywhere near this guy.

00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:11.203
Just look what happened to Rudy.

00:16:11.203 --> 00:16:12.837
He was already
under criminal investigation.

00:16:12.837 --> 00:16:14.506
Now he could get charged
for inciting a riot.

00:16:14.506 --> 00:16:16.909
He might get kicked out of the
New York State Bar Association,

00:16:16.909 --> 00:16:18.677
and he hasn't been watered
in months.

00:16:18.677 --> 00:16:20.979
Every soulless Republican today
who accommodated

00:16:20.979 --> 00:16:23.348
this obviously deranged
president for four years,

00:16:23.348 --> 00:16:26.017
every spineless factotum
who carried out the business

00:16:26.017 --> 00:16:28.186
of keeping the institutional
Republican Party

00:16:28.186 --> 00:16:29.287
aligned with Trump

00:16:29.287 --> 00:16:30.789
shares in the destruction
they've wrought

00:16:30.789 --> 00:16:32.791
and the shame
that comes with it.

00:16:32.791 --> 00:16:34.526
And we all have to reckon
with the fact

00:16:34.526 --> 00:16:36.561
that this isn't going away.
Trump's not unique.

00:16:36.561 --> 00:16:38.964
He's not alone.
He's the emblem and embodiment

00:16:38.964 --> 00:16:41.867
of the modern Republican Party.
If they want to fix that,

00:16:41.867 --> 00:16:43.835
the bare minimum they can do
is cast him out

00:16:43.835 --> 00:16:46.238
and disqualify him from
ever holding office again.

00:16:46.238 --> 00:16:48.006
But even then
the rot Trump exposed

00:16:48.006 --> 00:16:50.342
will remain throughout the GOP,
from Fox News

00:16:50.342 --> 00:16:53.378
to Lindsey Graham
to Rudy Giuliani to...

00:16:53.378 --> 00:16:54.980 line:14%
-The guy from My Pillow.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.081
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

